[
  {
    "start": 0.0,
    "end": 6.68,
    "text": "And if you don't make these simplifications, then when you get, say, a dozen of them together,",
    "s_text": 0.6248,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 6.68,
    "end": 8.84,
    "text": "you can't figure out what's going on.",
    "s_text": 0.566,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 8.84,
    "end": 12.76,
    "text": "In this case, the design of the satellite, it's very important.",
    "s_text": 0.6381,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0863,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 12.76,
    "end": 18.0,
    "text": "This speed actually isn't just one speed, because it's the relative speed of you to the",
    "s_text": 0.606,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 18.0,
    "end": 22.36,
    "text": "the satellite, and you might be at a, it depends on your angle of sight with the satellite,",
    "s_text": 0.6445,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1642,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 22.36,
    "end": 23.36,
    "text": "what the speed is.",
    "s_text": 0.4909,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.4826,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 23.36,
    "end": 24.36,
    "text": "So it varies quite a bit.",
    "s_text": 0.4787,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3378,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 24.36,
    "end": 26.36,
    "text": "So you really need this rule of thumb.",
    "s_text": 0.658,
    "s_visual": 0.3721,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3107,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 26.44,
    "end": 30.68,
    "text": "Then there are all kinds of other considerations in this question like, for example, there's",
    "s_text": 0.6533,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.4973,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 30.68,
    "end": 35.28,
    "text": "the fact that we're sitting on Earth, and so we're rotating around what's called a non-neutral",
    "s_text": 0.6302,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3946,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 35.28,
    "end": 36.44,
    "text": "frame.",
    "s_text": 0.2917,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3588,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 36.44,
    "end": 39.04,
    "text": "So there's the question of that acceleration.",
    "s_text": 0.6474,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3542,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 39.04,
    "end": 43.0,
    "text": "There's the question that the gravity that I experience here on Earth is not the same",
    "s_text": 0.5069,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.4255,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 43.0,
    "end": 48.88,
    "text": "as up at the satellite, and that also creates a difference in time as a result of general",
    "s_text": 0.6043,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.2979,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 48.88,
    "end": 49.88,
    "text": "relativity.",
    "s_text": 0.1856,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1828,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 49.88,
    "end": 56.08,
    "text": "So all of these considerations come down to formulas, which are this complicated or maybe",
    "s_text": 0.7536,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0627,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 56.08,
    "end": 58.56,
    "text": "a tiny bit more, not really that much.",
    "s_text": 0.4035,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.2155,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 58.56,
    "end": 62.4,
    "text": "And then people simplify them enormously to these very simple-minded rules, and then",
    "s_text": 0.5263,
    "s_visual": 0.0,
    "visual_reliability": 0.5177,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 62.4,
    "end": 65.32,
    "text": "they keep track of what's going on.",
    "s_text": 0.5791,
    "s_visual": 0.1873,
    "visual_reliability": 0.8766,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 65.32,
    "end": 69.44,
    "text": "So in order to design the system, you must make these simplifications, otherwise you",
    "s_text": 0.6607,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.6136,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 69.44,
    "end": 72.08,
    "text": "can't even think about what's going on.",
    "s_text": 0.433,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.2105,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 72.08,
    "end": 78.08,
    "text": "I mean, this comes up in everything, in weather forecasting, economic forecasting, figuring",
    "s_text": 0.5171,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3941,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 78.08,
    "end": 81.72,
    "text": "out whether there's going to be an asteroid that's going to hit the Earth.",
    "s_text": 0.4512,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3871,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 81.72,
    "end": 86.04,
    "text": "Because every single one of these things involves dozens of these considerations.",
    "s_text": 0.493,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3693,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 86.04,
    "end": 90.56,
    "text": "Okay, there was a question that I saw here, yes.",
    "s_text": 0.4599,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3452,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 90.56,
    "end": 103.88,
    "text": "Yeah, so in basically any problem where you have a derivative, the rate of change also",
    "s_text": 0.6366,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.4204,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 103.88,
    "end": 106.36,
    "text": "depends on what the base point is.",
    "s_text": 0.6649,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1442,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 106.36,
    "end": 107.36,
    "text": "That's the question.",
    "s_text": 0.5939,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 107.36,
    "end": 109.72,
    "text": "You're saying, doesn't this delta V also depend?",
    "s_text": 0.4466,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0797,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 109.8,
    "end": 111.16,
    "text": "I had a base point in that problem.",
    "s_text": 0.5586,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0634,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 111.16,
    "end": 115.72,
    "text": "I happened to decide that pictures pitch on average about 90 miles an hour.",
    "s_text": 0.478,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3499,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 115.72,
    "end": 119.76,
    "text": "Whereas in fact, some pictures pitch at 100 miles an hour, some pictures at 80 miles an",
    "s_text": 0.3488,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1714,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 119.76,
    "end": 122.32,
    "text": "hour, and of course they vary the speed of the pitch.",
    "s_text": 0.4595,
    "s_visual": 0.1591,
    "visual_reliability": 0.5048,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 122.32,
    "end": 123.68,
    "text": "And so this varies a little bit.",
    "s_text": 0.5408,
    "s_visual": 0.4347,
    "visual_reliability": 0.6873,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 123.68,
    "end": 125.44,
    "text": "In fact, that's sort of a second order effect.",
    "s_text": 0.5538,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.5327,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 125.44,
    "end": 128.48,
    "text": "It does change the constant of proportionality.",
    "s_text": 0.5401,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3909,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 128.48,
    "end": 133.92,
    "text": "It's a rate of change at a different base point, which we're considering fixed.",
    "s_text": 0.499,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.2462,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 133.92,
    "end": 134.92,
    "text": "Okay?",
    "s_text": 0.2483,
    "s_visual": 0.0103,
    "visual_reliability": 0.5773,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 134.92,
    "end": 139.12,
    "text": "In fact, if that's sort of a second order effect, when you actually do the computations",
    "s_text": 0.6341,
    "s_visual": 0.4348,
    "visual_reliability": 0.7275,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 139.12,
    "end": 142.76,
    "text": "where you discover is it doesn't make that much difference to the A.",
    "s_text": 0.7028,
    "s_visual": 0.4805,
    "visual_reliability": 0.7115,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 142.76,
    "end": 148.28,
    "text": "And that's something that you get from experience that it turns out that which things matter",
    "s_text": 0.5925,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.5782,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 148.28,
    "end": 149.28,
    "text": "and which things don't.",
    "s_text": 0.4131,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3896,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 149.28,
    "end": 153.44,
    "text": "And yet again, that's exactly the same sort of consideration, but at the next order of",
    "s_text": 0.6662,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1336,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 153.44,
    "end": 156.8,
    "text": "what I'm talking about here is you have to have enough experience with numbers to know",
    "s_text": 0.6151,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 156.8,
    "end": 160.8,
    "text": "that if you take, if you vary something a little bit, it's not going to change the answer",
    "s_text": 0.6722,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 160.8,
    "end": 162.8,
    "text": "that you're looking for very much.",
    "s_text": 0.5109,
    "s_visual": 0.1742,
    "visual_reliability": 0.4434,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 162.8,
    "end": 165.68,
    "text": "And that's exactly the point that I'm making.",
    "s_text": 0.5689,
    "s_visual": 0.178,
    "visual_reliability": 0.5074,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 165.68,
    "end": 170.08,
    "text": "So I can't make them all at once, all such points.",
    "s_text": 0.4603,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1741,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 170.08,
    "end": 171.6,
    "text": "All right.",
    "s_text": 0.5108,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0597,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 171.6,
    "end": 176.64,
    "text": "So that's my pitch for understanding things from this point of view.",
    "s_text": 0.6948,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 176.64,
    "end": 193.52,
    "text": "Now we're going to go on now to quadratic approximations, which are a little more complicated.",
    "s_text": 0.6428,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 193.52,
    "end": 198.32,
    "text": "So we talked a little bit about this last time, but I didn't finish, so I want to finish",
    "s_text": 0.7061,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 198.32,
    "end": 200.28,
    "text": "this up.",
    "s_text": 0.5293,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.2775,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 200.28,
    "end": 210.4,
    "text": "And the first thing that I should say is that you use these when the linear approximation",
    "s_text": 0.6962,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1942,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 210.4,
    "end": 214.76,
    "text": "is not enough.",
    "s_text": 0.3853,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1562,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 214.76,
    "end": 216.76,
    "text": "Okay?",
    "s_text": 0.2483,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0536,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 216.76,
    "end": 220.52,
    "text": "So that's something that you really need to get a little experience with.",
    "s_text": 0.6249,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 220.52,
    "end": 224.12,
    "text": "In economics, I told you they use logarithms.",
    "s_text": 0.4711,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1575,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 224.12,
    "end": 226.44,
    "text": "So sometimes they use log linear functions.",
    "s_text": 0.36,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1519,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 226.44,
    "end": 230.08,
    "text": "Sometimes they use log quadratic functions when the log linear ones don't work.",
    "s_text": 0.3275,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0521,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 230.08,
    "end": 234.0,
    "text": "So most modeling in economics is with log quadratic functions.",
    "s_text": 0.556,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1117,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 234.0,
    "end": 238.32,
    "text": "And if you made it any more complicated than that, it's useless and it's a mess and people",
    "s_text": 0.5614,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.48,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 238.32,
    "end": 239.32,
    "text": "don't do it.",
    "s_text": 0.4105,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.4341,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 239.32,
    "end": 242.0,
    "text": "So they stick with the quadratic ones, typically.",
    "s_text": 0.491,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3334,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 242.0,
    "end": 243.0,
    "text": "All right.",
    "s_text": 0.5108,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1144,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 243.0,
    "end": 249.08,
    "text": "So the basic formula here, and I'm going to take the base point to be zero, is that f",
    "s_text": 0.7554,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.2449,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 249.08,
    "end": 254.92,
    "text": "of x is approximately f of zero plus f prime of zero times x.",
    "s_text": 0.4611,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.084,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 254.92,
    "end": 259.44,
    "text": "That's the linear part, plus this extra term, which is f double prime of zero divided",
    "s_text": 0.6776,
    "s_visual": 0.0,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3419,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 259.44,
    "end": 261.8,
    "text": "by two x squared.",
    "s_text": 0.2486,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.5035,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 261.8,
    "end": 266.96,
    "text": "And this is supposed to work for x near zero.",
    "s_text": 0.566,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.2272,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 266.96,
    "end": 267.96,
    "text": "Okay?",
    "s_text": 0.2483,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0779,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 267.96,
    "end": 272.28,
    "text": "So I've chosen the base point as simply as possible.",
    "s_text": 0.4947,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.4009,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 272.28,
    "end": 274.4,
    "text": "All right.",
    "s_text": 0.5108,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3455,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 274.4,
    "end": 278.2,
    "text": "So here's more or less where we left off last time.",
    "s_text": 0.5386,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.2219,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 278.2,
    "end": 285.04,
    "text": "And one thing that I said I was going to explain, which I will now, is why it's a half",
    "s_text": 0.766,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1289,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 285.04,
    "end": 288.6,
    "text": "f double prime of zero.",
    "s_text": 0.4354,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 288.6,
    "end": 291.76,
    "text": "So we need to know that.",
    "s_text": 0.7066,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 291.76,
    "end": 293.92,
    "text": "So let's work that out here.",
    "s_text": 0.6463,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 293.92,
    "end": 297.52,
    "text": "First of all, so I'm just going to do it by example.",
    "s_text": 0.7403,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 297.52,
    "end": 303.72,
    "text": "So if you like, the answer is just, well, what happens when you have a parabola?",
    "s_text": 0.5695,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 303.72,
    "end": 306.8,
    "text": "A parabola is a quadratic.",
    "s_text": 0.3594,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 306.8,
    "end": 310.6,
    "text": "It had better, its quadratic approximation had better be itself.",
    "s_text": 0.4434,
    "s_visual": 0.4817,
    "visual_reliability": 0.4422,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 310.6,
    "end": 313.16,
    "text": "It's got to be the best one, so it's got to be itself.",
    "s_text": 0.6036,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.4041,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 313.16,
    "end": 319.92,
    "text": "So this formula, if it's going to work, has to work on the button, on the nose, for",
    "s_text": 0.7055,
    "s_visual": 0.2,
    "visual_reliability": 0.3318,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 319.92,
    "end": 322.08,
    "text": "quadratic functions.",
    "s_text": 0.2243,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1877,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 322.08,
    "end": 323.92,
    "text": "So let's take a look.",
    "s_text": 0.5415,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0644,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 323.92,
    "end": 328.28,
    "text": "If I differentiate, I get b plus 2cx.",
    "s_text": 0.2199,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 328.28,
    "end": 332.48,
    "text": "If I differentiate a second time, I get 2c.",
    "s_text": 0.1812,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 332.48,
    "end": 334.88,
    "text": "And now let's plug it in.",
    "s_text": 0.7001,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 334.88,
    "end": 337.96,
    "text": "Well, we can recover.",
    "s_text": 0.4867,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 337.96,
    "end": 339.6,
    "text": "What is it that we want to recover?",
    "s_text": 0.6022,
    "s_visual": 0.1701,
    "visual_reliability": 0.2632,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 339.6,
    "end": 348.92,
    "text": "We want to recover these numbers, a, b and c, using the derivatives evaluated at zero.",
    "s_text": 0.6167,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.1843,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 348.92,
    "end": 349.92,
    "text": "So let's see.",
    "s_text": 0.5764,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0632,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 349.92,
    "end": 351.04,
    "text": "It's pretty easy actually.",
    "s_text": 0.3572,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 351.04,
    "end": 352.88,
    "text": "f of zero is a.",
    "s_text": 0.475,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 352.88,
    "end": 353.88,
    "text": "That's on the nose.",
    "s_text": 0.5723,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 353.88,
    "end": 358.28,
    "text": "If you plug in x equals zero here, these terms drop out, you get a.",
    "s_text": 0.5443,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 358.28,
    "end": 362.4,
    "text": "And now f prime of zero, whoops, that was wrong.",
    "s_text": 0.6075,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 362.4,
    "end": 365.56,
    "text": "So I wrote f prime, but what I meant was f.",
    "s_text": 0.5098,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 365.56,
    "end": 367.96,
    "text": "So f of zero is a.",
    "s_text": 0.5496,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 367.96,
    "end": 369.16,
    "text": "It's back up.",
    "s_text": 0.4314,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 369.16,
    "end": 370.0,
    "text": "f of zero is a.",
    "s_text": 0.475,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 370.0,
    "end": 373.24,
    "text": "So if I plug in x equals zero, I get a.",
    "s_text": 0.4629,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 373.24,
    "end": 377.72,
    "text": "Now f prime of zero, that's this next formula here.",
    "s_text": 0.6586,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 377.72,
    "end": 381.36,
    "text": "f prime of zero, I plug in zero here, and I get b.",
    "s_text": 0.4861,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 381.36,
    "end": 382.4,
    "text": "That's also good.",
    "s_text": 0.458,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 382.4,
    "end": 385.72,
    "text": "And that's exactly what the linear approximation is supposed to be.",
    "s_text": 0.694,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 385.72,
    "end": 388.68,
    "text": "But now you notice f double prime is 2c.",
    "s_text": 0.5653,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 388.68,
    "end": 394.68,
    "text": "So to recover c, I better take half of it.",
    "s_text": 0.5545,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 394.68,
    "end": 395.48,
    "text": "And that's it.",
    "s_text": 0.7547,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 395.48,
    "end": 398.16,
    "text": "That's the reason.",
    "s_text": 0.6573,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 398.16,
    "end": 400.84,
    "text": "There's no chance that any other formula could work.",
    "s_text": 0.2884,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 400.84,
    "end": 404.76,
    "text": "And this one does.",
    "s_text": 0.5934,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 404.76,
    "end": 410.44,
    "text": "All right, so that's the explanation for the formula.",
    "s_text": 0.7065,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 410.44,
    "end": 415.32,
    "text": "And now I remind you that I had a collection of basic formulas written on the board.",
    "s_text": 0.7416,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 415.32,
    "end": 420.92,
    "text": "And I want to just make sure we know all of them again.",
    "s_text": 0.6564,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 420.92,
    "end": 427.72,
    "text": "So first of all, there was sine x is approximately x.",
    "s_text": 0.5757,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 427.72,
    "end": 432.76,
    "text": "Cos sine x is approximately 1 minus 1 half x squared.",
    "s_text": 0.3358,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 432.76,
    "end": 439.48,
    "text": "And e to the x is approximately 1 plus x plus 1 half x squared.",
    "s_text": 0.6188,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 439.48,
    "end": 442.4,
    "text": "So those were three that I mentioned last time.",
    "s_text": 0.5649,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 442.4,
    "end": 451.32,
    "text": "And again, this is all for x near 0, all for x near 0 only.",
    "s_text": 0.5311,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 451.32,
    "end": 455.44,
    "text": "These are wildly wrong far away, but near 0, they're",
    "s_text": 0.5425,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.0699,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 455.44,
    "end": 457.88,
    "text": "nice good quadratic approximations.",
    "s_text": 0.2308,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 457.88,
    "end": 465.12,
    "text": "Now the other two approximations that I want to mention are the logarithm.",
    "s_text": 0.5721,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 465.12,
    "end": 470.6,
    "text": "And we use the base point shifted so we can put it at x near 0.",
    "s_text": 0.5507,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 470.6,
    "end": 475.56,
    "text": "And this one, sorry, this isn't approximately equals sine there.",
    "s_text": 0.5201,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 475.56,
    "end": 479.64,
    "text": "Turns out to be x minus 1 half x squared.",
    "s_text": 0.3964,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 479.64,
    "end": 486.0,
    "text": "And the last one is 1 plus x to the power r, which",
    "s_text": 0.6068,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 486.0,
    "end": 494.6,
    "text": "turns out to be 1 plus r x plus r times r minus 1 divided by 2 x squared.",
    "s_text": 0.4062,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 494.6,
    "end": 500.08,
    "text": "Now eventually, your mind will converge on all of these.",
    "s_text": 0.7001,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 500.08,
    "end": 503.52,
    "text": "And you'll find them relatively easy to memorize.",
    "s_text": 0.496,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 503.52,
    "end": 505.96,
    "text": "But it'll take some getting used to.",
    "s_text": 0.5698,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 505.96,
    "end": 511.6,
    "text": "And I'm not claiming that you should recognize them and understand them all now.",
    "s_text": 0.6582,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 511.6,
    "end": 515.44,
    "text": "But we're going to put a giant box around this.",
    "s_text": 0.6591,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 519.28,
    "end": 519.44,
    "text": "Yeah.",
    "s_text": 0.3776,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 519.44,
    "end": 521.68,
    "text": "Are you getting all of these?",
    "s_text": 0.5791,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 521.68,
    "end": 522.52,
    "text": "Yeah.",
    "s_text": 0.3776,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 522.52,
    "end": 525.8,
    "text": "So the question was, you get all of these that you use that equation in.",
    "s_text": 0.7837,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 525.8,
    "end": 527.8,
    "text": "That's exactly what I'm going to do.",
    "s_text": 0.5519,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 527.8,
    "end": 532.44,
    "text": "So I already did it actually for these three last time.",
    "s_text": 0.5728,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 532.44,
    "end": 535.96,
    "text": "But I didn't do it yet for these two.",
    "s_text": 0.462,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 535.96,
    "end": 538.8,
    "text": "But I will do it in about two minutes.",
    "s_text": 0.5229,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 538.8,
    "end": 540.44,
    "text": "Well, maybe five minutes.",
    "s_text": 0.2443,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 540.44,
    "end": 546.44,
    "text": "But first, I want to explain just a few things about these.",
    "s_text": 0.5779,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 546.44,
    "end": 546.94,
    "text": "OK?",
    "s_text": 0.2441,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 550.48,
    "end": 553.0,
    "text": "All right, they all follow from the basic formula.",
    "s_text": 0.4912,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 553.0,
    "end": 555.84,
    "text": "In fact, that one deserves a pink box too.",
    "s_text": 0.4302,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 556.84,
    "end": 557.92,
    "text": "That one's pretty important.",
    "s_text": 0.563,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 557.92,
    "end": 559.88,
    "text": "All right.",
    "s_text": 0.5108,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 559.88,
    "end": 560.88,
    "text": "Yeah.",
    "s_text": 0.3776,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 563.12,
    "end": 565.16,
    "text": "Maybe even some little sparkles.",
    "s_text": 0.2279,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 569.84,
    "end": 572.92,
    "text": "All right.",
    "s_text": 0.5108,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 572.92,
    "end": 575.28,
    "text": "OK, so that's pretty important.",
    "s_text": 0.6482,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 575.28,
    "end": 576.48,
    "text": "All right.",
    "s_text": 0.5108,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 576.48,
    "end": 580.92,
    "text": "Almost as important as the more basic one without this term here.",
    "s_text": 0.5653,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 580.92,
    "end": 581.28,
    "text": "All right.",
    "s_text": 0.5108,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 581.28,
    "end": 588.68,
    "text": "So now let me just tell you a little bit more about the significance.",
    "s_text": 0.646,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 594.84,
    "end": 597.72,
    "text": "Again, this is just to reinforce something that we've already done.",
    "s_text": 0.716,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  },
  {
    "start": 597.72,
    "end": 600.08,
    "text": "But it's closely related to what you're doing on your product.",
    "s_text": 0.7079,
    "s_visual": 0.1,
    "visual_reliability": 0.05,
    "teaching_stage": "semantic"
  }
]